# Design and Content Contributions

This document summarizes my contributions to the visual presentation and content organization of **DevConnect**, a developer community project.

Project: [DevConnect](https://github.com/divanshi046/devconnect)  
Live demo: [divanshi046.github.io/devconnect](https://divanshi046.github.io/devconnect/)

## Visual Design

- Developed a warm blush-and-cream visual direction with editorial typography and a consistent color palette.
- Designed the landing page presentation, including the headline, supporting copy, navigation, and calls to action.
- Created the architectural hero illustration with CSS shapes and visual details.
- Organized feature cards to introduce the community’s core themes: sharing work, meeting developers, and collaborating.
- Applied the visual style across the community workspace, including feed cards, profile content, project cards, and navigation.
- Supported responsive layouts and light/dark theme presentation.

## Content Management

- Organized the community feed around developer updates, code snippets, and project posts.
- Structured profile content such as role, location, bio, GitHub link, skills, achievements, and project details.
- Added clear labels and supporting copy for the community’s main areas, including Explore, Connections, Messages, and Team Finder.
- Curated sample developer posts and project descriptions to demonstrate the kinds of content members can share.
- Maintained consistent text style and content hierarchy across the landing page, feed, profiles, and project sections.

## Project Areas

- `index.html` — landing page, feature content, app shell, and profile form structure
- `styles.css` — visual presentation, responsive layouts, components, and themes
- `app.js` — feed content, demo data, page rendering, and interactions
- `features.js` — team finder, notifications, GitHub profile details, and profile extras

## Note

DevConnect is a browser-based community app prototype. Its sample posts and profiles demonstrate the product’s content features; they are not presented as real user-generated content.
